sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant API@{ "type": "control" } as Dictaphone API
    participant Reencoder@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP re-encoding worker
    participant Validator@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP validation worker
    participant DB@{ "type": "database" } as PostgreSQL
    participant Queue@{ "type": "queue" } as Redis and Celery queue
    participant Backend@{ "type": "control" } as Backend worker
    participant FileStore@{ "type": "database" } as File-linked object storage
    participant Summary@{ "type": "boundary" } as Summary service

    Reencoder->>API: GET /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/transcoding/next<br/>Bearer token
    API-->>Reencoder: Job id, expires_at, source_url, destination_url
    Reencoder->>FileStore: Fresh attempt child: GET source_url, transcode with FFmpeg,<br/>PUT destination_url
    Reencoder->>API: POST /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/transcoding/complete<br/>id and status<br/>duration_seconds on success or error on failure
    API->>DB: Record transcoding result and duration<br/>make validation job available on success
    Validator->>API: GET /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/validation/next<br/>Bearer token
    API-->>Validator: Job id, expires_at, source_url
    Validator->>FileStore: Fresh attempt child: GET source_url<br/>and validate with opusinfo + opusdec
    Validator->>API: POST /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/validation/complete<br/>id, status, error on failure
    API->>DB: Record successful validation attempt<br/>derived state becomes EXTRACTION_DONE<br/>persist transcription intent
    API->>Queue: call_transcribe_service.delay(file_id, ai_job_id)<br/>after commit, queue: dictaphone-backend
    Queue->>Backend: call_transcribe_service(file_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-backend
    Backend->>DB: Load PENDING transcription job<br/>and its validated audio attempt
    Backend->>FileStore: Generate signed GET URL for derived audio
    Backend->>Summary: POST /api/v2/async-jobs/transcribe

    alt Transcription request failure
        Summary-->>Backend: Request failure
        Backend->>DB: Mark transcription job FAILED
    else Transcription request succeeds
        Summary-->>Backend: 200 pending and remote job id
        Backend->>DB: Save remote transcription job id
    end

    Note over Reencoder,Validator: This sequence shows claimed tasks on the successful path.<br/>Empty queues wait and poll again, each Deployment stops new claims after 15 minutes.<br/>Attempt isolation, failure paths, deadlines, and health probes are detailed in the worker diagrams.
